{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-fix-fmt-sort/fmt2b-ix-dup-ladder",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-FMT-2",
    "II-05 Splits / stable root",
    "II-05 Statistics word",
    "II-03 concrete mutation probes"
  ],
  "description": "Repairs r-fmt-2b/ix-dup-ladder: no public read between steps (only the whole-file hash existed for the middle steps). Inserts into a non-unique index that holds one value many times: IxD has 300 rows (ID 1..300) all with G = 7 and index IX_IxD_G on G. Four single statements add 100, 100, 200 and 400 more rows with G = 7. Asks at which statement the duplicate-key index gains pages and how the primary-key index and the statistic change; count and the index statistics are read back after each statement. Images: 'before' (the fixture copy as given), then one kept image of the closed file after each step; every step opens the database read/write, makes its mutation and closes it, with the DBEngine still alive.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
